#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SE2307 expect=violation domain=FW
#note "column-absent case on the second in-scope domain: FWENDY is not present as a column at all, so the bare empty(--ENDY) leaf is TRUE on every row (absent = all-missing, EC-43) -> the rule fires even though FWDY is populated. Plan B phase 4d' deleted the not var_exists(--ENDY) disjunct that used to spell this out; the verdict is unchanged. Verdict-only: the firing condition is a pure column-absence fact, which the engine reports once per dataset rather than per row, so no row= pin is asserted here."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset FW class=FINDINGS label="Food and Water Consumption"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col FWSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col FWTESTCD type=Char label="Food/Water Consumption Short Name"
col FWDY     type=Num  label="Study Day of Start of Observation"
---
S1 | FW | 001 | 1 | FCONSUM | 1
S1 | FW | 001 | 2 | FCONSUM | 8
